  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "UK garage two-step: the kick leaves the second and fourth beat, skipping to the and of three, under a snare on two and four, swung sixteenth hats and a syncopated sub",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "Two bars: kick one and the and of three, then one, the a of two and the and of three; snare on two and four with a rim-like ghost before the second; sixteenth hats swung hard (0.62, the shuffle) with the offbeat louder; a quiet shaker; a sub that pushes the and of one and answers itself in the second bar, inside a fifth. At 130 under the Tech House key: garage has no key of its own, and 130 is the fast band's top."
  }
